Note on the proving toolchain
-----------------------------

`@soldsoul86/circuit` depends on snarkjs and circomlibjs, and its build step
uses the circom compiler and circomlib. Those are GPL-3.0. That package is
therefore the one piece of this repository whose distribution terms are not
simply Apache-2.0, and anyone redistributing it should take their own advice
on the combination.

It is a separate package for exactly this reason. `@soldsoul86/policy` and
`@soldsoul86/journal` have **no third-party runtime dependencies at all**, and
depending on them pulls in nothing GPL-licensed. `@soldsoul86/anthropic` adds
only a peer dependency on the Anthropic SDK, which it uses for its types and
never imports at runtime. `@soldsoul86/x402` adds a runtime peer dependency on
`@x402/core`, Apache-2.0, for the client hooks and header codecs.

That absence was not an accident. The engine that decides whether money moves
was kept dependency-free so it could run anywhere, offline, with nothing
installed -- and a clean licensing position is a welcome side effect of the
same decision.
